OL,3,GNEWSABelfast Telegraph bomb victim
OL,4,Aremembered on 50th anniversary
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe granddaughter of a Belfast
OL,7,FTelegraph worker killed 50 years ago
OL,8,Fsays it is important to remember
OL,9,F"forgotten" victims of violence.
OL,11,FWhen the offices of the newspaper were
OL,12,Fbombed on 15 September 1976, it was the
OL,13,Fattack on the media that grabbed the
OL,14,Fheadlines.
OL,16,FFour days later, one of those injured
OL,17,Fin the blast, 63-year-old printer
OL,18,FJoseph Paton from Lisburn, died in
OL,19,Fhospital.
OL,23,APub: 14-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NI NewsC Reg TVF On This Day
